---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
export const prerender = true;

const updated = 'August 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="Shipping, returns and terms"
  description="Shipping, returns and terms for Diving Diaries sticker orders."
>
  <section class="relative overflow-hidden bg-ocean-900 text-white">
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-br from-ocean-900 via-ocean-950 to-purple-900/70"></div>
    <div class="relative mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 pb-14 pt-32">
      <p class="kicker text-purple-200">The small print</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl sm:text-5xl">Shipping, returns and terms</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-ocean-100">Last updated {updated}.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-16">
    <div class="prose-dd space-y-10 text-slate-600 [&_p]:mt-4 [&_p]:leading-relaxed">
      <div id="shipping">
        <h2>Shipping</h2>
        <p>
          Shipping is a flat <strong>$1.50</strong> on every order, however many stickers
          you buy. We post within Australia only at the moment.
        </p>
        <p>
          Orders are packed by hand and usually go in the post within a couple of days.
          They travel as ordinary letter mail, so allow up to a week or so for it to
          arrive depending on where you are. Letter mail is not tracked.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div id="returns">
        <h2>Returns and refunds</h2>
        <p>
          We do not accept returns for change of mind. Stickers are a small, low cost
          item and once they have been posted they cannot be resold.
        </p>
        <p>
          If your order arrives <strong>genuinely damaged</strong>, get in touch and we
          will sort it out. Every case is looked at individually, and depending on what
          happened that means a replacement or a refund.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Tell us within 15 days</strong> of your order arriving. Email
          <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>, mention the name on the
          order, and send a photo of the damage if you can. The photo is the quickest
          way to get it resolved.
        </p>
        <p>
          None of this limits your rights under Australian Consumer Law, which applies
          no matter what this page says.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div id="terms">
        <h2>Terms</h2>
        <p>
          Diving Diaries sells printed vinyl stickers to customers in Australia. Prices
          are in Australian dollars and include no GST, as the business is not currently
          registered for it.
        </p>
        <p>
          Payment is handled by <strong>Stripe</strong>. We never see or store your card
          details. Your name, email and postal address are used to process and post your
          order, and for nothing else. We do not sell or share them.
        </p>
        <p>
          Stock counts on the shop are kept by hand. In the unlikely event something sells
          out between your order and packing it, we will contact you and refund you in
          full.
        </p>
        <p>
          The artwork and the Diving Diaries name remain ours. Buying a sticker does not
          transfer any right to reproduce or resell the designs.
        </p>
        <p>
          Questions about any of this? Email
          <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
